  "worked_solution": "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$30$** | **$25$** | **$20$** | **$15$** | **$12$** |\n| ${x}_{3}$ | **$2$** | **$6$** | **$12$** | **$20$** | **$30$** |\n| $y$ | $-10$ | $-6$ | $0$ | $4$ | $10$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the hyperplane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}_{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 30 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 25 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 20 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 15 & 20 \\\\ 5 & 12 & 30\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.",
